  "title": "Colouring knots exist exactly on Gallai trees and compose by fusion",
  "subject": "Composition of K1-K3 knots through hidden witness networks in the proper colouring law",
  "conclusion": "In the q-colouring law, hidden witnesses with q neighbours each give their visible leaves a K1-K3 knot exactly when the witness graph is a Gallai tree; otherwise they impose nothing. Gluing at a witness fuses two knots into one with multiplicative excluded mass, and a shared visible vertex is a hub, so knots here compose by fusion along Gallai trees, never into networks of distinct knots.",
